From: MOSS Windows lane <moss@example.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A working directory seclogon turned down on a local drive is not a mapped drive

---

Upstream: anthropics/sandbox-runtime, tag v0.0.81 (c40cf14), after 0001-0004.
Reason: spawn_runner turned ANY ERROR_DIRECTORY from CreateProcessWithLogonW into the typed
mapped_drive_cwd error ("C:\ is DRIVE_REMOTE ..."), whatever the drive was. A folder that was removed, or
that the sandbox account may not enter, was reported to the person as a mapped drive. Now the post-check
asks GetDriveTypeW: a remote drive is still mapped_drive_cwd (exit 16); anything else is cwd_unusable
(exit 27), carrying the cwd, the HRESULT, whether the caller's own token sees the folder, and the
drive type.

